==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|litter bug|litter-bug}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|litter|bug}}.  Coined in 1947 by New York copywriter Paul B. Gioni for The American Ad Council.<ref>{{cite-web |title=Ad Council : Pollution: Keep America Beautiful - Iron Eyes Cody (1961-1983) |url=http://www.adcouncil.org/default.aspx?id=132 |accessdate=10 July 2018 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20081030084003/http://www.adcouncil.org/default.aspx?id=132 |archivedate=30 October 2008 }}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪtɚˌbʌɡ/|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A person who tends to drop [[litter]] and not clean it up.
#: {{syn|en|litter lout}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1967|author=w:Arlo Guthrie|title=w:Alice's Restaurant|passage={{...}} I mean I'm sittin' here, on the Group W bench, 'cause you want to know if I'm moral enough to join the army, burn women, kids, houses and villages, after being a '''litterbug'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Sam Roberts|title=John J. Doherty, Stalwart Sanitation Commissioner, Dies at 84|work=The New York Times|date=2023-04-18|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/18/nyregion/john-j-doherty-dead.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Mr. Doherty was known to publicly berate '''litterbugs''' and upbraid motorists whose stranded cars prevented plows from clearing snow.}}

